      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are passing these values as `size_t` parameters to functions such as `malloc()` and `memset()`, so these strides and heights cannot be negative.\n\nThe problem with using `int64_t` is that in 32-bit systems it needs to be converted to the 32-bit `size_t` type, but there is no check to ensure the `int64_t` values are \u003c\u003d `SIZE_MAX`. So we might as well use the `size_t` type directly. In these tests the operands are all small constants so their products won\u0027t overflow 32-bit `size_t`, otherwise we would need to exclude these tests in 32-bit builds.",
      "parentUuid": "1f1407d3_384879a4",
